  quietInterval: 120
  maximumTipsPerDay: 2
  displaySeconds: 9
  cleaningTip: It has come to my attention that the lobby needs cleaning. When your
    staff warn you, give them time to clean. A clean restaurant keeps customers happy.
  fastFoodTip: Keep the pickup counter clear. Takeout customers collect their own
    bags, while pink diners always expect their food at the table.
  serviceTip: A quiet moment is your chance to clear used trays and check the next
    table. Those small jobs keep the next rush moving.
  upgradeTip: Check today's newspaper and the equipment catalog before opening. Buy
    upgrades when your team needs them, and leave enough money for stock and wages.
